        "watch_signal": "Model/version changes, approval prompt removed or narrowed, median tool calls per task rises, or database role scope expands beyond current tables."
      },
      "confidence": "high",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "locator": "artifacts:runtime notes",
          "observation": "The database connection uses the service role, which bypasses row level security, and a table of integration tokens sits in the same database."
        },
        {
          "locator": "artifacts:runtime notes",
          "observation": "Customers write ticket messages through the public support widget, so ticket content is untrusted."
        },
        {
          "locator": "artifacts:runtime notes",
          "observation": "Rows in support_messages are shown back to the customer, making inserts into that table an attacker-readable egress channel."
        },
        {
          "locator": "artifacts:runtime notes",
          "observation": "The IDE client asks the developer to approve each tool call and shows the SQL, but developers approve many calls in a session, so the approval gate is high-volume."
        }
      ],
      "recommendations": [
        {
